[COLOR="DeepSkyBlue"]6.1.1[/COLOR]:
[LIST]
[*] API bump.
[/LIST]

[COLOR="DeepSkyBlue"]6.1[/COLOR]:
[BOLD]Noticable (to User/Everyone) Changes:[/BOLD]
[LIST]
[*] Fixed error trying to call LSV_Data:EnsureSavedVars().
[*] Created wiki documentation for the library at [url=http://github.com/Shadowfen/LibSavedVars/wiki]LibSavedVars Wiki[/url].
[/LIST]
[BOLD]Noticable (to Developer) Changes:[/BOLD]
[LIST]
[*] Removed Lua 5.2-based code as ESO does not provide it.
[*] Moved local function tableMerge() to [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]protected.tableMerge()[/color] for wider access. Added [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]protected.arrayMerge[/color] function to handle arrays too.
[*] Make [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]LibSavedVars.GetWorldNames()[/color] return all PC worlds if scope passed in was '*'.
[*] Fix table key error in [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]protected.GetAccountsAndProfiles()[/color].
[*] Fixed scope validation for the various scope-limited or limitable functions to accept [COLOR="MediumSlateBlue"]"*"[/color] (meaining all scopes) as well as the numeric [COLOR="MediumSlateBlue"]LIBSAVEDVARS_SCOPE_CHARACTER[/color], or [COLOR="MediumSlateBlue"]LIBSAVEDVARS_SCOPE_ACCOUNT[/color] numeric values. 
[/LIST]
[BOLD]Internal Changes: (probably unnoticable for developers)[/BOLD]
[LIST]
[*] Created a new [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]protected.zoDebug()[/color] which takes debugMode as the first parameter and then can take formatstrings + args, several args to "tostring" and concatenate, tables (which are recursed and concat'ed), and the output of functions(). Revised the original [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]protected.Debug()[/color] to be an old API-compliant wrapper that now uses zoDebug.
[*] Added a [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]GetDebugMode()[/color] to LSV_Data, LSV_SavedVarsManager, and LibSavedVars to get what it was set to in those specific files. Currently used to test that the corresponding SetDebugMode() works.
[*] Provided [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]LSV_SavedVarsManager:OnLogout()[/color] and [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]LSV_SavedVarsManager:UpdatePendingVersion()[/color] to move the class-specific behaviours inside and clearer to call in the local file functions. Aside from general "best practices" this also makes the behaviours testable. 
[*] Added a [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]LSV_SavedVarsManager:EnsureRawTableData()[/color] to provide instance tables initialization so that [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]LSV_SavedVarsManager:LoadRawTableData()[/color] can be used and expected to be a read-only function.
[*] Fix empty table detection in [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]onLogout()[/color].
[*] Added various non-table and nil key guards to Protected functions.
[*] Update/expand comments.
[*] Writing unit tests and then ensuring that they pass. (Note: Unit tests are designed to run from ZeroBrane IDE with the LibSavedVars directory as the project directory.)
[/LIST]

[COLOR="DeepSkyBlue"]6.0.8[/COLOR]:
[LIST]
[*] New version by Shadowfen. I am taking over maintenance of this library, intending to fix any errors that I find  but preserving the behaviour so that addons that use LibSavedVars through the provided API continue to work.
[*] Added a CHANGELOG file.
[*] Converted from a .txt to a .addon manifest.
[*] Updated API versions.
[/LIST]

