[COLOR="DeepSkyBlue"]Version 5.0.1[/color]
- Update 24 Dragonhold API bump

[COLOR="DeepSkyBlue"]Version 5.0.0[/color]
- Update 23 Scalebreaker compatibility. This version is compatible with both Update 22 Elsweyr and Update 23.
- Removed LibStub support. Simply refer to the library by the LibSavedVars global now.
- Improved German tooltip for the "Account-Wide" LibAddonMenu checkbox (thanks, Baertram!)

[COLOR="DeepSkyBlue"]Version 4.2.2[/color]
- Fix for character-scope settings not receiving new default saved vars values when they are only specified at the account-level.

[COLOR="DeepSkyBlue"]Version 4.2.1[/color]
- Fix for error being thrown when LibStub is not installed

[COLOR="DeepSkyBlue"]Version 4.2.0[/color]
- Remove LibStub dependency
- Add new global LibSavedVars for addon authors to use instead of LibStub
- Add ESO - Japanese Localization addon compatibility

[COLOR="DeepSkyBlue"]Version 4.1.0[/color]
- API bump for Update 22 Elsweyr
- Marked as library in manifest with new ## IsLibrary flag.

[COLOR="DeepSkyBlue"]Version 4.0.1[/color]
- Fix load order problem with older versions

[COLOR="DeepSkyBlue"]Version 4.0.0[/color]

- Added saved vars version support that does not wipe all settings during upgrade. See classes/LSV_Data.lua:
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]RemoveSettings()[/color]
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]RenameSettings()[/color]
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]RenameSettingsAndInvert()[/color]
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]Version()[/color]

- Changed constructor method names and parameters to match ZO_SavedVars exactly. See LibSavedVars.lua:
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]NewAccountWide()[/color]
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]NewCharacterSettings()[/color] / [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]NewCharacterIdSettings()[/color]

- Added new chainable methods for adding account or character-specific saved vars toggle. See classes/LSV_Data.lua:
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]AddAccountWideToggle()[/color]
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]AddCharacterSettingsToggle()[/color]

- Added several new helper methods:
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]GetAccountsAndProfiles(savedVarName)[/color]: Gets a list of tables of the form { account = "@displayName", profile = "NA Megaserver" } for all accounts within the given saved var table.
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]GetInfo(savedVars)[/color]: Gets table containing information about the given saved vars, such as addon name, constructor parameters, raw saved vars table, etc.

- Migration no longer requires creating a ZO_SavedVars instance or leaves any data behind in the legacy saved vars tables. See LibSavedVars.lua:
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]MigrateAccountWide()[/color]
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]MigrateCharacterId()[/color]
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]MigrateCharacterName()[/color]
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]MigrateCharacterNameToId()[/color]
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]MigrateToMegaserverProfiles()[/color]

- Deprecated the following methods in LibSavedVars.lua:
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]New()[/color]. See [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]NewAccountWide()[/color] and [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]NewCharacterSettings()[/color]
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]GetClass()[/color]. You can now access classes directly by name (e.g. LSV_Data, LSV_SavedVarsManager)

- Deprecated the following methods in classes\LSV_Data.lua (formerly just Data.lua):
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]New()[/color]. See [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]NewAccountWide()[/color] and [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]NewCharacterSettings()[/color].
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]Migrate()[/color]. See MigrateFrom().

- Moved Lua 5.2 pairs(), ipairs() and next() overrides into a separate library, LibLua5.2, to avoid the performance penalty for non-developers or anyone else who doesn't care about iterating saved vars.

- API bump for Update 21 Wrathstone

[COLOR="DeepSkyBlue"]Version 3.0[/color]

- New methods [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]New()[/color], [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]NewAccountWide()[/color] and [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]NewCharacterIdSettings()[/color] return a data object that can be used as a 1:1 replacement for ZO_SavedVars instances
- New helper method [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]GetRawDataTable() returns the underlying data table for a ZO_SavedVars instance, since [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]ZO_SavedVars:New() just returns an interface, not the data itself.
- Added usage documentation / comments to all public methods in code.

- Data class features:
* data["key"] and data.key operator support
* data["key"] = value and data.key = value operator support
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]next()[/color], [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]pairs()[/color] and [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]ipairs()[/color] support for iterating saved vars
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]GetAccountSavedVarsActive()[/color] and [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]SetAccountSavedVarsActive(value)[/color] methods for toggling the active scope between account and character-specific settings
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]Migrate(legacySavedVars, beforeCallback, addon, ...)[/color] method to call directly and control when migration is executed.
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]GetActiveSavedVars()[/color] method to return a reference to the active ZO_SavedVars instance for the currently logged-in character
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]GetLength()[/color] returns the # length of the data for the active ZO_SavedVars instance for the currently logged-in character
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]GetLibAddonMenuAccountCheckbox()[/color] replaces the old library-wide method that took an "addon" parameter.

- DEPRECATED METHODS:
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]Get()[/color] Use data["key"] or data.key of the new data class instead.
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]Set(value)[/color] Use data["key"] = value or data.key = value of the new data class instead.
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]Init()[/color] Legacy var migration moved to data class. Use [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]data:Migrate() of the new data class and [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]New()[/color], [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]NewAccountWide()[/color] and [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]NewCharacterIdSettings()[/color] instead.
* [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]GetLibAddonMenuSetting(addon)[/color] Use [COLOR="MediumSeaGreen"]data:GetLibAddonMenuSetting()[/color] of the new data class instead.


[COLOR="DeepSkyBlue"]Version 2[/color]
- Fix bug where account wide settings overwrite character settings when toggling in LAM2

[COLOR="DeepSkyBlue"]Version 1[/color]
